WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.685 --> 00:00:13.731
"Our house looks amazing!"

2
00:00:14.251 --> 00:00:14.891
a woman said.

3
00:00:16.312 --> 00:00:17.133
Her husband nodded.

4
00:00:17.153 --> 00:00:19.514
"I can't wait to go inside."

5
00:00:20.715 --> 00:00:23.396
A big man in overalls and a hard hat stood nearby.

6
00:00:23.416 --> 00:00:25.217
"Go in," he said.

7
00:00:25.237 --> 00:00:27.098
"You're going to love it."

8
00:00:28.699 --> 00:00:29.440
The couple went in.

9
00:00:31.244 --> 00:00:32.225
The wife gasped.

10
00:00:33.687 --> 00:00:36.650
"Everything is crooked!"

11
00:00:38.672 --> 00:00:39.893
The husband scratched his head.

12
00:00:39.913 --> 00:00:42.837
"The builder did a terrible job!"

13
00:00:43.938 --> 00:00:46.561
As he turned to go back outside, the floor opened up.

14
00:00:46.981 --> 00:00:49.244
The couple screamed and tumbled into darkness.

15
00:00:58.592 --> 00:01:01.354
"Ugh! I'm so tired of this dreary rain!"

16
00:01:01.674 --> 00:01:02.274
Mara said.

17
00:01:03.215 --> 00:01:05.096
Roxy and her friends were on their way to school.

18
00:01:05.816 --> 00:01:08.958
The sky was filled with gray clouds, and rain was falling lightly.

19
00:01:08.978 --> 00:01:11.440
"Me too," Roxy said.

20
00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:14.221
"It feels like it's been raining for weeks.

21
00:01:14.822 --> 00:01:15.842
I miss the sun."

22
00:01:15.862 --> 00:01:17.963
"I like the rain."

23
00:01:18.964 --> 00:01:20.565
Jack looked up and held his mouth open.

24
00:01:21.085 --> 00:01:22.626
He caught some raindrops on his tongue.

25
00:01:23.747 --> 00:01:25.548
Terrell wiped raindrops off his glasses.

26
00:01:26.112 --> 00:01:29.294
"Well, I hate when it rains all day long," he said.

27
00:01:29.314 --> 00:01:34.738
"It means—" "Indoor recess!"

28
00:01:35.358 --> 00:01:36.479
Mara said with a groan.

29
00:01:36.499 --> 00:01:40.322
"Indoor recess stinks," Jack said.

30
00:01:40.982 --> 00:01:42.043
He stomped in a puddle.

31
00:01:42.543 --> 00:01:43.864
Water splashed everywhere.

32
00:01:43.884 --> 00:01:46.246
"It's so boring!"

33
00:01:48.187 --> 00:01:49.188
Rain fell harder now.

34
00:01:50.689 --> 00:01:52.010
The friends walked more quickly.

35
00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:55.072
Heavy raindrops drummed against their umbrellas.

36
00:01:56.128 --> 00:01:59.570
"At least it will be quiet in school today," Mara said.

37
00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:02.852
"The construction work is finally done."

38
00:02:04.813 --> 00:02:07.654
Workers had been at school every day for the past three weeks.

39
00:02:08.775 --> 00:02:11.937
Principal Penn had said the building was old and needed some repairs.

40
00:02:14.338 --> 00:02:15.859
Terrell shot a quick look at Roxy.

41
00:02:15.879 --> 00:02:19.041
"I hope Rocket Girl doesn't have to do anything today."

42
00:02:20.161 --> 00:02:20.922
Mara looked over.

43
00:02:20.942 --> 00:02:23.323
"Why?" Terrell shrugged.

44
00:02:24.003 --> 00:02:24.704
"It's raining.

45
00:02:25.296 --> 00:02:27.678
It must be hard to fight villains in the rain."

46
00:02:28.699 --> 00:02:29.380
Jack laughed.

47
00:02:30.901 --> 00:02:31.561
"No way!

48
00:02:31.742 --> 00:02:33.283
Rocket Girl is super tough.

49
00:02:33.523 --> 00:02:34.664
Rain doesn't bother her."

50
00:02:36.085 --> 00:02:38.227
Roxy shot a quick look at Terrell and smiled.

51
00:02:38.247 --> 00:02:40.068
"I agree with Terrell.

52
00:02:40.349 --> 00:02:43.551
Rocket Girl probably doesn't want to get soaked while fighting villains."

53
00:02:45.873 --> 00:02:47.875
When they reached the school, Roxy's watch beeped.

54
00:02:51.058 --> 00:02:53.640
She sneaked away from her friends and stood close to the building.

55
00:02:55.436 --> 00:02:56.858
"Mayor Bloom," she said.

56
00:02:56.878 --> 00:02:58.199
"What's wrong?"

57
00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:01.242
The mayor had a worried look on his face.

58
00:03:01.262 --> 00:03:04.485
"I'm not sure if anything is wrong, Rocket Girl.

59
00:03:04.846 --> 00:03:08.049
But I tried to call Detective Smith, and he didn't answer his phone.

60
00:03:08.649 --> 00:03:10.872
I can't reach any other police officers either.

61
00:03:11.412 --> 00:03:13.234
I'm worried that something happened to them."

62
00:03:13.254 --> 00:03:16.297
"Don't worry, Mayor," Roxy said.

63
00:03:16.317 --> 00:03:18.680
"I'll find out what's going on."
